{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.SurfaceExponentIsDimension","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Asymptotics"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.deltahedronSurface_not_hasBulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.deltahedronSurface_not_hasBulk","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L228-L230","doc":"The convex deltahedron's surface count fails the criterion, for the opposite reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.chainSurface_not_hasBulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.chainSurface_not_hasBulk","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L224-L226","doc":"The chain's surface count fails the criterion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.powerSurface_hasBulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.powerSurface_hasBulk","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L210-L222","doc":"**A sublinear power surface count has a bulk** — the compact-packing case, where the\n`θ = 2/3` of `CoordinationSurfaceDeficit` lives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.linearSurface_not_hasBulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.linearSurface_not_hasBulk","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L200-L208","doc":"**A surface count proportional to `A` has no bulk** — the convex deltahedron's case, where\nevery nucleon is a hull vertex. The surface grows, but there is no interior, so the deficit\nrenormalises the volume term and contributes no `A`-dependence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.boundedSurface_not_hasBulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.boundedSurface_not_hasBulk","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L193-L198","doc":"**A constant surface count has no bulk** — the chain's case, `A_surf = 2`. There is an\ninterior but the surface does not grow, so the deficit is a fixed number of missing bonds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.HasBulk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.HasBulk","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L187-L191","doc":"**An edge set has a bulk** when its surface count grows without bound — there *is* a\nsurface — while the surface *fraction* vanishes — there *is* an interior. Each clause alone is\ncheap; the conjunction is the content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.deltahedron_is_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.deltahedron_is_affine","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L180-L183","doc":"The deltahedron contact graph `E = 3A − 6` (Euler, `2E = 3F`) is affine at `α = 3, β = −6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.chain_is_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.chain_is_affine","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L174-L178","doc":"The production word's chain is affine at `α = 1, β = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.affine_ne_surfaceLaw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.affine_ne_surfaceLaw","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L163-L172","doc":"**No affine bond count is a surface law.** For `ε ≠ 0` and `β ≠ 0`, the affine law differs\nfrom the `p` law with the same amplitude at some `A > 0`, for every `p ≠ 1`. The exponent is the\nobstruction; no choice of `α`, `β` or `ε` removes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.affine_eq_perNucleonExp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.affine_eq_perNucleonExp","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L155-L161","doc":"**Every affine bond count is the `p = 1` member of the family**, whatever `α` and `β` are. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.affine_perNucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.affine_perNucleon","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L149-L153","doc":"**An affine bond count's per-nucleon binding is `εα + εβ/A`, exactly.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.affineBondCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationBulkCriterion.affineBondCount","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationBulkCriterion.lean#L146-L147","doc":"A bond count affine in the mass number: `M(A) = α·A + β`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}